      <memberdef kind="function" id="classAsyncDbClient_1ac0396c3d59602cf860e6fef52c98a736" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>std::shared_ptr&lt; drogon::orm::DbClient &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::shared_ptr&lt; drogon::orm::DbClient &gt; AsyncDbClient::createClient</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>createClient</name>
        <qualifiedname>AsyncDbClient::createClient</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Builds a Drogon PostgreSQL client from the configuration held in the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Creates the Drogon Pg client from the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref>&apos;s database configuration.</para>
<para>Reads <computeroutput><ref refid="classConfigurator_1afdc97f6e9bd19c0197759b8860ed9a49" kindref="member">Configurator::DatabaseConfig</ref></computeroutput> from the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref>, builds the connection string with <computeroutput><ref refid="classAsyncDbClient_1a060a2df97483204c119b2d3322de7455" kindref="member">connectionString</ref></computeroutput>, requests <computeroutput>DB_MAX_CONN</computeroutput> connections and applies the acquire timeout, converting milliseconds to the seconds Drogon expects. <simplesect kind="return"><para>A newly created client, ready to be wrapped and registered with <computeroutput><ref refid="classStore_1a1e12f060c02095975351db8f5d63cb76" kindref="member">Store::registerObject</ref>&lt;<ref refid="classAsyncDbClient" kindref="compound">AsyncDbClient</ref>&gt;</computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para>A <computeroutput><ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref></computeroutput> object is registered in the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref>.</para>
</simplesect>
<computeroutput>newPgClient</computeroutput> receives the generated connection string and <computeroutput>DB_MAX_CONN</computeroutput>; the timeout is then set from <computeroutput>DB_ACQUIRE_TIMEOUT_MS</computeroutput>. Any connection-establishment work is left to Drogon. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
