        <name>connectionString</name>
        <qualifiedname>AsyncDbClient::connectionString</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="classConfigurator_1afdc97f6e9bd19c0197759b8860ed9a49" kindref="member">Configurator::DatabaseConfig</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>config</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Renders a libpq keyword/value connection string from a database configuration. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Formats the libpq connection string, mapping <computeroutput>config.ssl</computeroutput> to <computeroutput>sslmode</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">config</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Source of host, port, database name, user, password and SSL settings. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><computeroutput>host=... port=... dbname=... user=... password=... connect_timeout=2 sslmode=require|disable</computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>The returned string contains the database password in clear text; it must not be logged. <computeroutput>printValues()</computeroutput> on the configuration deliberately redacts the same field.</para>
</simplesect>
<computeroutput>connect_timeout</computeroutput> is a fixed two seconds, independent of DB_* tuning; host and SSL settings may be overridden by the container image but still arrive through this one configuration object. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
