    <briefdescription>
<para>Store-registered holder for the Drogon PostgreSQL client used when DB_ASYNC=true. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The wrapper holds a <computeroutput>shared_ptr&lt;drogon::orm::DbClient&gt;</computeroutput>; production instances are created from the DB_* settings. <computeroutput><ref refid="classServer_1a30362b937b125d27916cf595bfc4c1a7" kindref="member">Server::run()</ref></computeroutput> registers it in the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref> only while <computeroutput>DatabaseConfig::async</computeroutput> is enabled; the synchronous pool stays in use while the flag is off. Callers fetch it with <computeroutput><ref refid="classStore_1a0607fb3b583c06ca910ed6c9881e790c" kindref="member">Store::getObject</ref>&lt;<ref refid="classAsyncDbClient" kindref="compound">AsyncDbClient</ref>&gt;(nullptr)</computeroutput> and hand the underlying client to <computeroutput><ref refid="namespaceasyncdb_1abf4af65046571ee330dc2320277a57f7" kindref="member">asyncdb::execSqlCoro</ref></computeroutput>. Tests replace the registered instance through <computeroutput><ref refid="classStore_1a2a4bfc0b18f2999216eda3067988cf57" kindref="member">Store::replaceObject</ref></computeroutput>; a null client is a valid state meaning &quot;async path unavailable&quot;, which the controller treats as <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput>. The wrapper itself is non-copyable and non-movable so there is a single long-lived Store-owned instance. It adds no locking of its own; any thread-safety comes from the underlying Drogon DbClient. <simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classAsyncDbClient_1ac0396c3d59602cf860e6fef52c98a736" kindref="member">createClient</ref>, <ref refid="namespaceasyncdb_1abf4af65046571ee330dc2320277a57f7" kindref="member">asyncdb::execSqlCoro</ref>, <ref refid="classDatabaseController_1a5874c6f56191991a88da60758f2200fa" kindref="member">DatabaseController::executeQueryCoro</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
